Description: Look up Qt6QmlIntegration on the top level before Qt6 Quick
 When kirigami is configured with cmake 4.3 under qemu-user (arm64 build on an
 amd64 host), the nested lookup of Qt6QmlIntegration from Qt6QmlDependencies.cmake
 sporadically fails although the package is installed ("Could NOT find
 Qt6QmlIntegration (missing: Qt6QmlIntegration_DIR)"). Finding it once on the top
 level sets Qt6QmlIntegration_FOUND, so the nested lookup is skipped. Build
 environment workaround only; no change to the built code.
Author: lisbon <lisbon@localhost>
Forwarded: not-needed
License: LGPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched file, debian/copyright "Files: *")
Last-Update: 2026-11-19
---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -33,6 +33,9 @@
 include(KDEInstallDirs)
 include(KDECMakeSettings)
 include(KDEFrameworkCompilerSettings NO_POLICY_SCOPE)
+# lisbon: look up QmlIntegration on the top level first; Qt6QmlDependencies.cmake then skips its nested lookup,
+# which sporadically misses the installed package when cmake runs under qemu-user
+find_package(Qt6QmlIntegration ${REQUIRED_QT_VERSION} REQUIRED NO_MODULE)
 find_package(Qt6 ${REQUIRED_QT_VERSION} REQUIRED NO_MODULE COMPONENTS Core Quick Gui Svg QuickControls2 Concurrent ShaderTools)
 
 if (Qt6Gui_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL "6.10.0")
